# The backend image's build context is this directory (see docker-compose.yml
# and backend/azure-pipelines.yml). It was the repository root until `docs/`
# moved in here; the root .dockerignore that went with that arrangement is gone,
# because no context is rooted there any more.
#
# Everything below is either rebuilt inside the image, has no business leaving
# the machine, or is test scaffolding the image does not need.
.dockerignore

# Credentials. Nothing below /app is COPYed from these paths, but the context is
# still handed to the daemon whole, and `.gitignore` says a real .env is where
# endpoint credentials live. The example file is documentation and stays.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The internal CA bundle. Gitignored, so it is absent on a clean checkout and
# present on every machine set up per the README's internal-CA instructions —
# which is exactly the case that matters, because `COPY . .` would otherwise
# bake it into the image.
#
# That image is also what the sandbox container runs, and the sandbox is
# supposed to hold no CA material at all (app/sandbox/__init__.py). Baking it in
# would put private-PKI material inside the container that executes uploaded
# code, and would do it only on the machines where there is something to leak.
#
# The backend still gets it, by the mount docker-compose.prod.yml already makes
# at /app/certs — which is the reason that mount exists rather than a rebuild.
certs/
!certs/README.md

# `**/`, and it is load-bearing rather than decoration. A .dockerignore pattern
# is matched against a file's whole path relative to the context root, so a bare
# `__pycache__/` excludes only one at the top level — and every one that matters
# is nested (app/__pycache__, app/sandbox/__pycache__, tests/__pycache__, all of
# which exist after a single local `pytest` run).
#
# Without the prefix those are handed to the daemon and copied in by `COPY . .`,
# which busts the source layer's cache on every local test run and ships one
# machine's bytecode inside the image — including the image the sandbox runs.
# The rules above are deliberately not prefixed: `.env` and `certs/` mean those
# files at the root of this directory and nowhere else.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.log
